## (1) listener release
`asio_tcp_listener.cpp:83` enables SO_REUSEPORT; on unbind/close the listener fd is closed on the I/O thread later (listener process_term). Make the fd close part of the
completion the caller observes (before ZLINK_CLOSE_OK / unbind returns) — the same rule as inproc — and remove the reliance on SO_REUSEPORT for rebind (keep it only if a
documented reason exists; say which). Check ipc and ws/tls listeners too. Contract test: close/unbind a tcp listener → immediately bind the same port from a new socket in the
same context → succeeds AND no connection is accepted by the old listener (connect after rebind lands on the new one); ×100 under load. Do not add a bind-side wait/retry.
## (2) inproc unbind latency
`socket_base_endpoint.cpp:969` (`terminate_inproc_pipe_with_peer_progress`) drives peer progress only for lane_count == 1, so the 20×10 ms handshake wait at `:1053-1061` is
consumed for 2-lane pairs (~200 ms per unbind). Drive the same progress for every lane count (one rule); test: ROUTER↔ROUTER inproc unbind completes in < 50 ms ×50, and the
existing unbind semantics (peer observes DISCONNECTED, pending requests NOT_FOUND per D-090/NOT_FOUND rule) hold.
